      "definition": {
        "@value": "The protocol stack or network stack is an implementation of a computer networking protocol suite or protocol family. Some of these terms are used interchangeably but strictly speaking, the _suite_ is the definition of the communication protocols, and the _stack_ is the software implementation of them.",
        "@language": "en"
      },
