        }
      ],
      "definition": {
        "@value": "Self-sovereign identity is a decentralized identity architecture that implements the Principles of SSI \u2014 principally that it puts the identity controller (e.g., a natural person or organization) directly in control of the identifiers and credentials they use to assert their digital identity.",
